From c6ea0a43ac081c8cea194f55a33de931f0ffb7c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix FoundFootage volume exception, casings vs. player, XM607
 ADS alignment

- FoundFootageController: reuse a component that already exists in the volume profile (TryGet) instead of
  VolumeProfile.Add() (InvalidOperationException), force overrideState so values apply, only destroy what it created.
- Casings ignore the player's colliders while in flight (and permanently with the big collider); once settled they
  get a tiny PlayerContact collider so the player only interacts with a much smaller object. Ejector wires it up.
- XM607 ADS: new WeaponController.alignRotationOnADS rotates the weapon to the camera axes (hip pose carried by
  WeaponSocket is yawed/pitched and rolled ~25deg; weapons without an ADS animation never levelled out).
- Optic aim points: Romeo Riser z 0.53 -> 0.628 (housing centre measured from mesh), x -> -0.002; T-1 Riser x -1.005 -> -0.002.
